{"name":"Coral Pink","hex":"#f88379","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many species of marine invertebrates in the class Anthozoa, most of which build hard calcium carbonate skeletons and form colonies, or a colony belonging to one of those species.","A hard substance made of the skeletons of these organisms."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of coral.","Having the orange-pink color of coral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coral (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The various tones of the color coral are orange, red and pink representations of the colors of those cnidarians known as precious corals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_(color)"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and secrete calcium carbonate to form a hard skeleton."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg/330px-Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black